    "created_at": "2016-08-17T15:50:30Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-08-17T15:50:30Z",
    "body": "Augh, I didn't pay enough attention to the OP here anyway.\n\nWrt the OP, `document.body.matches('body::after')` definitely returns false as currently specified.  \"Evaluate the selector\" ends up returning _just_ the body's ::after pseudo-element, and then \"match the selector against an element\" doesn't find `<body>` in the list, so you get false, as expected.  So, DOM doesn't need to do anything here.\n\n`querySelector()` does need to pass an empty list of allowed pseudo-elements, tho, since otherwise you get nonsensical results (there's no way to reflect a pseudo-element as a JS object right now).\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
